            content: `The Primals did not have a justice system. Justice systems require shared values, and Primals did not share values so much as they shared existence. But they had consensus. And in the weeks after the child disappeared, a consensus formed that required no debate.

Any being born in Limbo with signs of dual Harmony-Chaos alignment—the blessing of both order and unmaking in the same body—was to be killed immediately upon identification.

The logic was simple. The child had possessed dual alignment. The child had ended three Primordials without meaning to. A being that can do that by accident is a category of problem no civilization can afford to leave unaddressed.

The law was not cruel. It was not even angry. It was the conclusion that the facts produced when a species old enough to think at geological scales considered them without noise.

No one knew if there would be others.

There would be exactly two. But not for a very long time.`,
