            content: `His daughter, Cith More—Core State Nature-Energy primary, Chaos-Dark secondary—had been his operational second for a decade.

She understood numbers in the way people understand numbers only after they have spent long enough watching numbers fail to account for everything that matters, and have learned to factor in what numbers cannot reach. She knew how to plan for the space between what the numbers said and what would actually happen.

When the twins committed their full remaining forces to the last Primal stronghold, she ran the numbers. She ran them several ways. She arrived at the same conclusion each time.

It was not a battle. It was an erasure.

She told her father.

He nodded. He had already arrived at the same conclusion by a different route.

She organized the evacuation.

The plan required two things: someone to open the route out, and someone to hold the line long enough for everyone to pass through it. The route required Mana—a hidden realm somewhere in Limbo, a pocket of the void that only a Conceptual of Magic could have carved and sealed. Some of the oldest surviving Primals had sensed him distantly over the years. He was somewhere. He was reachable.

Cith More would lead the evacuation force toward that position.

Cycla More would hold the door open behind them with everything he had left.

They both understood what this meant. They did not spend time on the understanding. There was no time.`,
